You have two buckets fib_a and fib_b, start them at 0 and 1.
Ask the user for a number n, then swap and add the buckets 
n minus 2 times, each time storing the sum in temp first.

Take the two buckets and keep replacing the bigger one with 
the remainder of dividing them until one becomes zero. 
Whatever is left is the GCD, show it.

Take fib_b and call it num. Assume it is prime with is_prime 1.
If it is smaller than 2 it is not prime.
Otherwise keep trying to divide it by d starting from 2,
stop when d squared exceeds num, if any division has no 
remainder mark it as not prime. Each step raise d by 1 
and recalculate d squared.

Take fib_b again and call it cx, count steps at 0.
If cx is even halve it, if odd triple it and add 1.
Keep going until cx reaches 1, each iteration add 1 to steps.
Show steps.

Finally take fib_b and check each of its 64 bits one by one
using a mask starting at 1 that doubles each step.
Every time the AND with the mask is not zero add 1 to bits.
Show bits.